From d63529ba9ecf55d58f150f37aa4a10d149d8e53c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Patrick Delaunay <patrick.delaunay@foss.st.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Feb 2024 14:17:10 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 0732/1695] drivers: stm32_tamp: enable monitoring in PWR for
 associated TAMPER

Add a link in TAMPER driver to activate the platform resources
for each internal TAMPER with the new function
stm32_activate_internal_tamper(), defined for stm32mp1 and stm32mp2
platform.

Today the only few internal tamper INT_TAMP1 and INT_TAMP2
are handled for SoC STM32MP13x, STM32MP15x and STM32MP25x:
request PWR driver to enable the voltage and temperature monitoring
with stm32mp_pwr_monitoring_enable() when the associated internal
TAMPER are activated or check RCC CSS activation.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ST downstream https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/optee_os.git 42893b88d63cd77fbd78342af68df33705460037 drivers: stm32_tamp: enable monitoring in PWR for associated TAMPER]
Signed-off-by: Patrick Delaunay <patrick.delaunay@foss.st.com>
